From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:23:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/61] NNS.ANOVA: omit missing values in the two-sample path

The multi-group path already applies na.omit() to every column, but the
two-sample path (control, treatment) passed NA straight into the mean and
partial-moment ratios. It used to return Certainty = NaN; with the ratio
functions now rejecting non-finite input it would stop with an internal
"`variable` must be finite." message. Drop NA from both samples first,
matching the multi-group path.

Before -> after, NNS.ANOVA(airquality$Ozone, airquality$Solar.R)$Certainty:
  NaN -> 6.080922e-05 (identical to calling it on na.omit() of both)

Results change only for inputs containing NA.
---
 R/ANOVA.R | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/R/ANOVA.R b/R/ANOVA.R
index 03c933b..5d1b4ee 100644
--- a/R/ANOVA.R
+++ b/R/ANOVA.R
@@ -101,7 +101,11 @@ NNS.ANOVA <- function(
     # with treatment
     if (any(class(control)   %in% c("tbl","data.table"))) control   <- as.vector(unlist(control))
     if (any(class(treatment) %in% c("tbl","data.table"))) treatment <- as.vector(unlist(treatment))
-    
+
+    # Missing values are omitted, as in the multi-group path (na.omit per column).
+    control   <- control[!is.na(control)]
+    treatment <- treatment[!is.na(treatment)]
+
     if (robust) {
       # ---------------------------
       # Robust path: resample pairs
